First of all, don’t copy paste your code trunk. Without your data, we usually can’t help.

It would be better to provide minimal reproducible example.

An example like this is more suitable:
x = rtree(10)
d = data.frame(label = c('t1', 't2'), location=c("GZ", "HK"))
ggtree(x) %<+% d + geom_tippoint(aes(color=location))

This is an issue of ggplot2, which always translate NA value as a separate category by default. Such behavior can be disable in scale_color_xxx, e.g. :
 ggtree(x) %<+% d + geom_tippoint(aes(color=location)) +
    scale_color_manual(values=c("red", "blue"), na.translate=F)

