Hi,

I'm trying to plot a tree + heatmap but the space available for the column labels is rather limited even with extreme reduction on fontsize and colnames_angle (they are names of phyla, so full words)

library(ggtree)
library(tidyverse)

dist <- read.csv("dist.csv", header = TRUE, row.names = 1)
dist1 <- as.dist(dist)
#View(dist1)
hc <- hclust(dist1)
den <- as.dendrogram(hc)

p <- ggtree(den)

mytable <- mytable <- read.csv("table.csv", header = T, row.names = 1)

gheatmap(p, mytable,
         low = "green", high = "red", color = "white",
         offset = .03,
         #font.size=2,
         colnames_angle=-15,
         hjust=0,
         colnames_position = "bottom", colnames_offset_y = 0) +
  geom_tiplab(size = 2)

Any idea, how to increase the space available for the column names?

Thank you in advance,
Xabi

