Hi Xabier,

You could try adding ‘’’+coord_fixed()’’’ to your code. This preserves the aspect ratio.

Then you can save the plot to whatever size you want using:
‘’’output_file=“myfile.pdf”
gg_save(output_file, width = 10, height = 7.5)’’’
Or whatever width and height numbers are good for you.

Basically your keeping the plot the same size but making the bounding box whatever size you want. This should be one way to solve the problem. I’m sure there are others!

